{{also|Appendix:Variations of "sur"}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|súrr}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*sūraz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*sūr-}}. Compare English {{m|en|sour}}, German {{m|de|sauer}}, Dutch {{m|nl|zuur}} Danish {{m|da|sur}}, Faroese {{m|fo|súrur}}, Norwegian {{m|no|sur}} and Swedish {{m|sv|sur}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/suːr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|uːr|lang=is}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|súrari|súrastur}}

# [[sour]], [[tart]], [[acid]], [[acidic]]
# (of mood) [[surly]], [[bitter]], [[morose]], [[sour]]
#: ''Ekki vera svona '''súr'''.''
#:: Don't be so '''morose'''.

